#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:1
msgid "Update a rendered scene in place"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:3
msgid "When data changes over time, such as colors that follow a time slider, rendering the whole scene again re-sends geometry that has not changed and rebuilds the render window. Instead, update just the actors that changed with {meth}`~pyvista_js.Plotter.update_actor`."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:8
msgid "In a notebook"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:10
msgid "Show the scene once:"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:24
msgid "Then, in a later cell, send new colors to it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:31
msgid "Actors are numbered in the order they were added. An update can:"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:33
msgid "add or replace point-data arrays with `point_data`,"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:34
msgid "color by a different point-data array with `scalars`,"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:35
msgid "move the points of a mesh given by points and faces with `points`."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:37
msgid "The number of points cannot change. The mesh is updated in Python too, so a page generated later shows the new data."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:40
msgid "In a page you embed yourself"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:42
msgid "If you put the page from {meth}`~pyvista_js.Plotter.generate_standalone_html` somewhere yourself, for example in an `<iframe>`, deliver the updates yourself as well. Pass `send=False` and serialize the message with {func}`~pyvista_js.rendering.scene_to_json`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:59
msgid "Then apply the message with `pvjsApplyUpdate`, which the page defines:"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:66
msgid "How the message gets to the page is up to you: a `postMessage` handler, a widget, or any other channel you already have."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:69
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:71
msgid "Updates reach the rendered mesh through smooth-shading normals, but not through filters such as {meth}`~pyvista_js.PolyData.clip` or {meth}`~pyvista_js.PolyData.contour`, which are computed when the page loads."
msgstr ""

#: ../howtos/update-in-place.md:74
msgid "`points` can only be updated for meshes given by points and faces, not for generated shapes such as {func}`~pyvista_js.Sphere`."
msgstr ""

